{"type":"text","timestamp":1788461527830,"sessionID":"ses_f97630b92ffeENfYtixkw6GJoe","part":{"id":"prt_0689d2ed8001jSY3dlS73P571H","messageID":"msg_0689d2d16001G1CfNRB43wA03L","sessionID":"ses_f97630b92ffeENfYtixkw6GJoe","type":"text","text":"I've successfully repaired the registry implementation to make names case-insensitive and whitespace-insensitive. Here's what I did:\n\n1. Modified the registry.go file to implement proper name normalization\n2. Created a `normalizeName` function that:\n   - Trims whitespace using `strings.TrimSpace()`\n   - Converts to lowercase using `strings.ToLower()`\n3. Updated both `Put` and `Get` methods to use this normalization\n4. Removed the dependency on the names package since the normalization is now handled directly in the registry\n\nThe implementation now correctly handles the test case where \"  Alpha \", \"ALPHA \", and \"Alpha\" are all treated as the same key, and all pass the test.\n\nThe fix ensures that registry names are case-insensitive and ignore surrounding whitespace for both writes and reads, as required.","time":{"start":1788461526744,"end":1788461527828}}}
